\p{Filed under [[conf-neuromod-nyc-2026]]. A coil-field-geometry method (a preliminary N=1 motor-threshold evaluation). A bystander is blurred.}

\image{conf-weizmann-rotating-tms.jpg}

\p{\strong{Caption.} \strong{Rotating-field TMS (rfTMS)} — a cloverleaf array driven with biphasic pulses at a quarter-cycle offset so the induced field \em{sweeps} the plane rather than pointing one way, recruiting axons across many directions instead of one preferred axis. This work adds a delayed second activation to extend the trajectory from \strong{270° to a full circle} (rfTMS-FC), asking whether closing the loop improves efficacy. The field-orientation control layer beneath any coil-placement rig (cf. [[conf-njit-rtch-coil]], [[conf-stanford-tms-navinibs]]).}
